FUN_0000_153c: thread the element-registrar's driver-filename-build + resource-open registers.

153c is the display-list ELEMENT registrar (main-menu path cae6 -> e714 -> e40e ->
e42f(type 0x30) -> 153c).  It builds an 8.3 filename at DGROUP:0x740 via the MGAVIDEO
name-table builder c550 (=driver 0x197) and opens it via the far vector DGROUP:0x388
(=FUN_1000_26fc, screen-resource OPEN).  Three __allregs indirect-vector arg-drops,
all threaded here faithfully from asm 0x151a..0x1552:
  loop c550 (asm 0x1524 `mov ax,0x24`): name-table[0x24]="MSPRITES.BIN" -> 0x197 digit
     "MSPRITE0.BIN" -> 153c loop patches [nul-5] with type digit (0x30 -> '6') ->
     "MSPRITE6.BIN".  Ghidra dropped ax -> name-table[0]="M1CON.MRL".  VERIFIED vs the
     real game (DOSBox open-trace): the menu opens exactly MSPRITE6.BIN here.  (The
     docs' "index 13 = MAINMENU.MRL" idea was a misdiagnosis; MAINMENU.MRL is a
     separate element.)
  post-loop c550 (asm 0x1549, ax=0xffff): 0x197 `cmp ax,0xffff; je skip` = NO-OP.
     Ghidra passed garbage 0 -> rebuilt "M1CON.MRL", clobbering the loop's name.
     Thread ax=0xffff so 0x197 skips.
  c388/26fc (asm 0x154f `mov dx,0x740; call [0x388]`): dropped dx/cx/bx.  26fc order
     (CX,DX,BX,BP); descriptor is at param_2:param_4, so thread cx=param_2, dx=0x740,
     bx=param_4.  Without dx the open used DS:DX=1c00:1c00 (empty name).
Result: 'MSPRITE6.BIN' -> ok on the real menu path.  Asm-verified 0x151a..0x1552.
